From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:07:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Sable locked glance, emergency shortcut and bouncer
 keyboard cues
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Completes the Sable lock screen design (sable-lockscreen-titan2,
LOCKSCREEN_SECURE_ENTRY_UX) on the legacy (blueprint) keyguard.
Credential checking, biometrics and trust are unchanged.

* Locked glance (SableLockGlanceSection, after the clock, date and
  notification sections of the default blueprint): "Locked" while the
  keyguard is secure and not unlocked; the Hub count row "2 Messages ·
  1 Mail · 1 Missed call" from the notifications the keyguard may show
  (KeyguardNotificationVisibilityProvider), by category (msg, email,
  missed_call) or, without a category, by known messaging and mail
  package; group summaries and ongoing notifications are not counted
  and the row is hidden when all counts are zero; the "Private mode ·
  Counts only until unlock" card when the user is in public mode and
  hides notification content; and "Open/reply requires unlock" under it
  while such notifications show. Counts only, no content read. Hidden
  while dozing. The notification stack starts below the glance. Pure
  policy: keyguard/sable/SableLockGlance.java.
* Emergency shortcut Alt+Space (either Alt; Sym is Right Alt on the
  Q25): opens the emergency dialer, or returns to a call, like the
  bouncer's Emergency button (SableEmergencyShortcut), from the lock
  screen and the bouncer. Handled pre-IME in KeyguardKeyEventInteractor
  so the password and PIN fields never see it, and its Space UP is
  consumed so it cannot also act as a confirm key. On the Q25 Space has
  no Alt digit and Sym pages only with E and R, so the chord never types
  a digit or pages. Only where the device can place calls.
* Hint line: "Enter unlock · Alt+Space emergency · ↑↓ notifications"
  for a PIN or password ("Enter unlock · ↑↓ notifications" without
  calling, "Enter unlocks · ↑↓ notifications" for swipe).
* Bouncer: second line "Physical keyboard active · Enter submits"; with
  a hardware keyboard the PIN field shows its focus ring (the upstream
  outline, also without pin_input_field_styled_focus_state) and the
  password field its focused background; a "Software keyboard fallback"
  line under the PIN keys and the password field.
* A notification whose content is hidden on the lock screen reads
  "N new · content hidden" next to its app name (the framework's
  redacted view only; an app's own public version is kept). N is the
  notification number or message count.

Tests: KeyguardKeyEventInteractorTest (Alt+Space), blueprint tests take
the new section.
